    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c176dcf0",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: the_name_s_todd_retodd; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image features a middle-aged man with a neutral expression, wearing a light-colored collared shirt, against a plain gray background. The text overlay reads \"the name's todd... retodd.\" This is a play on the classic James Bond introduction, but with a pun on the word \"retard\" (a highly offensive and derogatory term for people with intellectual disabilities). The meme uses the juxtaposition of a seemingly ordinary person with the text to create a humorous or mocking effect, implying the person is somehow 'retarded' or intellectually disabled. This is a harmful meme because it uses a slur to mock or demean individuals with intellectual disabilities, which can cause emotional harm and perpetuate stigma. The intent is to elicit laughter through the use of a derogatory term, but this comes at the expense of a vulnerable group and can be deeply offensive and hurtful to those affected.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_1ec781e5"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
